# Run from bugs/import_above_invocation/app:
#   kanso run .        fails: cannot resolve import "../../shared"
#   kanso run "$PWD"   prints "shared"
#
# Should: resolve the same import the same way however the entry directory
# is spelled on the command line. Does: resolve_import walks `../` lexically
# up the path it was given, so from a relative `.` it runs out of
# components one level early and looks for `../shared` beside the working
# directory instead of `shared` beside `app`. inner/ imports "../../shared":
# one `../` from inner/ is app/, the second is the directory holding app/
# and shared/.
import "./inner"

inner/hello
